prompt:
Use Three.js rendering + the Rapier 3D physics engine to implement a rigid-body stacking scene with mouse shooting.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Place the following import map in <head> (included verbatim), and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:

<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>

[Rapier Loading]
Use the CDN:
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.14.0/rapier.js
Call RAPIER.init() before creating the World (in accordance with the official documentation).

[Scene]
(1) A static ground (an infinite or large planar rigid body), with its normal pointing upward;
(2) 10 dynamic cubic rigid bodies, each with dimensions 1×1×1, stacked vertically, with center heights at y = 0.5, 1.5, …, 9.5, respectively;
(3) Gravity (0, -9.81, 0);

[Shooting Interaction]
(4) Mouse click: launch a spherical rigid body from the current camera position toward the intersection point between the ray and the scene (radius may be chosen freely, mass = 5.0), with an initial speed of 20 m/s (along the ray direction);
(5) The sphere must collide with the boxes and the ground;

[HUD (Required)]
(6) id="boxCount" displays the current number of boxes (initially 10);
(7) id="fallenCount" displays the number of boxes that have "fallen/left the stack" (the implementation must provide an explicit criterion, such as the center of mass falling below a certain height or the horizontal displacement exceeding a threshold);
(8) id="fps" displays the frame rate;
(9) id="resetBtn" button: after reset, restack 10 boxes, clear or recycle the spheres, and reset fallenCount to zero;

[State Exposure (Required, Updated Every Frame)]
window.__3D_STATE__:
  - boxCount: number
  - fallenCount: number
  - boxes: array, each item { x, y, z } representing the center-of-mass or center world coordinates of each box
  - sphereCount: current number of active launched spheres
  - fps: number (consistent with the HUD)

[Camera]
(10) OrbitControls or an equivalent viewpoint control, making it easy to aim at the stacked tower.

Output a single HTML file that can run when opened directly in a browser (network access is required to load the CDN resources).
